Sure!  The "while" loop is an "action is executed until the condition becomes false" loop.  For example, here’s a while loop that continues to print out the numbers from 1 to 10:

while (x > 0) {
   printf("%d\n", x);
   x--;
}

If you want to execute the code inside the loop, you need to use the "continue" statement.  Here’s an example:

int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
   printf("%d\n", i);
   i++;
   if (i > 5) {
       continue;
   }
}

